/* VaCuus M3 data-binding demo - stylesheet.

   RENDERER SUBSET, same as m1_hud.rcss and m2_demo.rcss and for the same reason:
   the M1 recorder implements solid fills (including alpha), 1px borders,
   border-radius as plain geometry, text, <img>, 2D transforms and scissor
   clipping. NO decorators/gradients, NO box-shadow, NO filter, NO transitions or
   animations (M5+). Nothing here scrolls, so the scissor/clip-mask trap m2_demo
   documents does not arise.

   RmlUi ships NO user-agent stylesheet -- there is not one .rcss file anywhere in
   Source/ThirdParty/RmlUi, and `display` is registered with a default of "inline"
   (ThirdParty/RmlUi/Source/Core/StyleSheetSpecification.cpp:306). So every tag
   that needs a box has to be told. */
div { display: block; }
span { display: inline; }

body
{
	display: block;
	width: 100%;
	height: 100%;
	font-family: LatoLatin;
	font-size: 16px;
	color: #D2E9F2;
}

#m3-title
{
	position: absolute;
	left: 48px;
	top: 36px;
	font-size: 26px;
	color: #7FE3FF;
}

/* The five panels, absolutely positioned so nothing here depends on flow rules the
   acceptance screenshot is not about. */
#p-scalars, #p-bar, #p-nested, #p-write, #p-kills
{
	position: absolute;
	left: 48px;
	width: 620px;
	padding: 14px 18px;
	background-color: #0A1A24E0;
	border: 1px #1E5A73;
	border-radius: 6px;
}

#p-scalars { top: 90px;  height: 168px; }
#p-bar     { top: 278px; height: 122px; }
#p-nested  { top: 420px; height: 100px; }
#p-write   { top: 540px; height: 132px; }

/* Section 5, the M3b killfeed: a SECOND column rather than a fifth row, because the first
   column already ends at y=672 and six 22px rows below it would fall off a 720-tall PIE
   viewport -- the same reason the left column's heights are what they are. Later in the file
   than the shared rule above so its left/width win the equal-specificity cascade. */
#p-kills { left: 700px; top: 90px; width: 470px; height: 186px; }

.panel-title
{
	color: #56C7E8;
	font-size: 14px;
	margin-bottom: 10px;
}

.row { height: 22px; }

.key
{
	color: #74909C;
	width: 190px;
	display: inline-block;
}

/* The value column. Every one of these is a `{{Field}}` substitution, so a stuck
   pipeline shows here as an unchanging or empty column rather than as an error. */
.val { color: #FFFFFF; }

/* data-class-alert="bAlert" adds and removes this class as the bool moves. The
   recolour is deliberately large: a class that never arrives is otherwise
   indistinguishable from one whose style is subtle. */
#p-scalars.alert
{
	background-color: #3A0B10E0;
	border: 1px #FF5A5A;
}

/* Section 2: the float rendered as geometry. #bar-fill's width is written by
   data-style-width, so its box really is laid out at the bound value -- which is
   why this is the panel a screenshot proves the most about. */
#bar-track
{
	width: 100%;
	height: 26px;
	margin-bottom: 10px;
	background-color: #102A38;
	border: 1px #1E5A73;
}

#bar-fill
{
	height: 24px;
	background-color: #2FD07A;
}

/* Section 4. A real <button>, i.e. interactive by tag, so the click that exercises
   the refused Set arrives through the ordinary input path. */
.m3-btn
{
	display: inline-block;
	padding: 6px 14px;
	margin-top: 4px;
	background-color: #14384A;
	border: 1px #2E7F9E;
	border-radius: 4px;
	color: #CFEFFA;
}

.m3-btn:hover  { background-color: #1D5570; }
.m3-btn:active { background-color: #2A7A9C; }
.m3-btn:focus  { border: 1px #7FE3FF; }

/* Section 5 rows. The template div itself never shows (DataViewFor::Initialize hides it,
   DataViewDefault.cpp:474); these style the generated clones, which carry the template's
   class list. Killer bright, victim white, weapon muted: the row has to read as
   "who > whom, with what" at screenshot size. */
.kill-row { height: 22px; }
.killer   { color: #7FE3FF; }
.k-sep    { color: #74909C; }
.victim   { color: #FFFFFF; }
/* margin-left, not source whitespace: the text between the template's child elements does
   not survive into the generated rows (checked on a real shot -- the weapon rendered glued
   to the victim), so the gap has to be the box's, not the document's. */
.weapon   { color: #74909C; font-size: 13px; margin-left: 8px; }

/* The HS pill. data-if toggles a LOCAL display:none against this rule's display
   (DataViewDefault.cpp:224-245), so inline-block here is the "true" state. Bordered and
   recolored for the m1_hud reason the alert class gives: a marker that never appears must
   not be confusable with one whose styling is merely subtle. */
.hs
{
	display: inline-block;
	color: #FF5A5A;
	border: 1px #FF5A5A;
	border-radius: 3px;
	font-size: 12px;
	padding: 0px 4px;
	margin-left: 6px;
}

#probe { color: #74909C; margin-bottom: 6px; }

.hint
{
	color: #5B7280;
	font-size: 13px;
	margin-top: 8px;
}
